#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087511 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "c7cc2dca-cc41-561c-bc48-bbcda272dd71" :question/math-academy-id "e-5792" :question/problem "The Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x)$. Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/896/Source/Images/19c7ba3bb7e7f5410bb6fd0adf39ce0e.png)" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_1= 2}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_{2,3}=-2\\pm \\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}a=1}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= a(x - x_{1})(x - x_{2})(x - x_{3}) \\\\\n&= (x - 2)(x - (-2 + \\textrm{i}))(x - (-2 - \\textrm{i}))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 2)(x - (-2 + \\textrm{i}))(x - (-2 - \\textrm{i})) &=  \\\\\n(x - 2)(x^{2} - x(-2 - \\textrm{i}) - x(-2 + \\textrm{i}) + (-2 + \\textrm{i})(-2 - \\textrm{i})) &=  \\\\\n(x - 2)(x^{2} + 4x + 5) &=  \\\\\nx^{3} + 4x^{2} + 5x - 2x^{2} - 8x - 10 &=  \\\\\n&= x^{3} + 2x^{2} - 3x - 10 \\mid\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf(x) = x^3+2x^2-3x-10\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087586 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "92ac2f4f-d0a5-5ccb-9213-87495927ccb8" :question/math-academy-id "e-8799" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=x_2=2,x_3=1$, and the coefficient of the cubic term is $3$. Find $P(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_1=x_2=2}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_3=1}\n$$\n\nand the coefficient of the cubic term is\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}a=3}\n$$\n\nwe can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(x - x_{1})(x - x_{2})(x - x_{3}) &= 3(x - 2)(x - 2)(x - 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3(x - 2)(x - 2)(x - 1) &= 3(x^{2} - 4x + 4)(x - 1) \\\\\n&= 3(x^{3} - x^{2} - 4x^{2} + 4x + 4x - 4) \\\\\n&= 3(x^{3} - 5x^{2} + 8x - 4) \\\\\n&= 3x^{3} - 15x^{2} + 24x - 12\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(x) = 3x^3 -15x^2+24x-12\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087906 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8db889c3-c19c-5637-8aef-e1488900d7f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} + 3x^{2} - 5x - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084448} {:answer/id #uuid "9b775426-0b4f-5aee-a02d-2ee9686862ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} - 6x^{2} - 2x + 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084449} {:answer/id #uuid "e449695a-8f8f-5e9f-a2a6-24133c819e3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} + 6x^{2} - 10x - 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084450} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd8afc3-e54c-54fa-9a89-624662056e76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} - x^{2} - 5x - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084451} {:answer/id #uuid "6688e61b-1b6d-5272-ac24-4f9f18d22e29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} - 2x^{2} - 10x - 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6688e61b-1b6d-5272-ac24-4f9f18d22e29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} - 2x^{2} - 10x - 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084452}